        "original_id": "fa245838-b21a-541f-9bb1-41d8f89831e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Erodium, Cymbidium, California macrophylla\n- Plant Families: Geraniaceae, Orchidaceae\n- Places: North Africa, Indomalaya, the Middle East, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Erodium is a genus of flowering plants in the family Geraniaceae.\n- Erodium includes about 60 species native to North Africa, Indomalaya, the Middle East, and Australia.\n- Cymbidium, also called boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the family Orchidaceae.\n- California macrophylla was formerly placed in the genus Erodium and was later moved to its own monotypic genus, California.",
